# Development: leave VITE_API_BASE_URL unset so the browser calls /api on the Vite
# dev host and vite.config.ts proxies to Laravel.
#
# Vite loads `.env.development` when you run `npm run dev` (see that file for defaults).
# If Laravel runs on another port (e.g. php artisan serve --port=8020), set:
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8020
#
# If you set VITE_API_BASE_URL to your Laravel URL, the browser calls the API
# directly — CORS must allow your Vite origin (see backend CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS).
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8020
#
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8020
